These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

npm's post gives its details about the incident. GitHub issue #116 is the original thread, where the payload unravelled and where Tarr answered the anger directed at him. Snyk published a post-mortem of the backdoor, and the fourth link is a systematic analysis of the incident. The MITRE page defines T1195.001, behind stage 02.

The background slides name their own sources: MITRE ATT&CK and the csoh.org glossary.

== Related kill chain and defense topics
layout: links
link: XZ Utils Backdoor 2024, the same route | breaches/xz-utils-backdoor.html
link: CI/CD and supply chain | ci-cd.html
link: Git and version control | version-control.html
link: Vulnerability management | vulnerability-management.html
